Out on the docking ring, a water-line tender drags a hose between two berths and does not look up. Vance Oduya watches Mira work his logs with the patience of a man who has been audited before. She finds the courier's departure entry and a second name beside it. Tarn Voss, a rigger she once crewed with, signed the fuel slip and stood at the lock as the courier cast off. The trail leads to the lower mooring tiers, where Tarn keeps a berth. Ren stays at the ring's rail, eyes on the approach lanes and the shuttles stacked there, counting who docks and who lingers. Vance clears his throat. "Voss owes half this station," he says. "He won't be glad to see you."

