"Keep your hands where he can see them," Vance mutters, though he is talking to nobody in particular. Ren leans in the hatchway and watches the dockmaster's fingers. They stay flat on the log board, too flat, until Mira turns a page. Then one thumb slides toward a switch under the lip of the desk, and stops. Vance notices Ren noticing. He lifts the hand slowly, rubs his jaw, and says nothing at all.

